4,Papua New Guinea Traditional Songs (1 Hour Compilation ...Abui [Newguineaworld]Top Tracks - Papua New Guinea - YouTube MusicMusic of Papua New Guinea - WikipediaLanguage: Abui (Makadai Dialect) - transnewguinea.orgAbui language - Wikipedia,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z05H4u8ZXNY,"Sep 19, 2025 · Papua New Guinea Traditional Songs (1 Hour Compilation) Tribal Music - Mamuna (Hypnotic) Perfect for: deep focus/work, mindful walking, meditation, breathwork, study, reading, nature... Abui is spoken in the central portion of Alor island of the Lesser Sunda chain in the Alor regency of Indonesia's East Nusa Tenggara province. The term Abui /abui/ [ˌʔɑbʊˈjɪ] means “mountain (s)/hill (s)” or “enclosed place.” Listen to Top Tracks - Papua New Guinea on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more. The music of Papua New Guinea encompasses a wide range of traditional and contemporary styles developed across the country's highly diverse ethnic groups. Traditional celebrations known as sing-sing feature communal song and dance, and form a central part of cultural life. Map: Resources: Glottolog page for Abui Ethnologue page for Abui Open Language Archives search for Abui Wikipedia page for Abui Multitree language relationships for Abui Glottolog resources for Abui Abui is a non-Austronesian language of the Alor Archipelago. It is spoken in the central part of Alor Island in Eastern Indonesia, East Nusa Tenggara (NTT) province by the Abui people. The native name in the Takalelang dialect is Abui tanga which literally translates as 'mountain language'.",Abui,Trans-New Guinea
